    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n34611" root="فم" body-key="f">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُمَّ</span></b>  a dial. var. of the conjunction <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُمَّ</span> [q. v.]:
(K:) or the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ف</span> in the former is a substitute for
the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ث</span> in the latter: one says, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">رَأَيْتُ عَمْرًا فُمَّ زَيْدًا</span>
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُمَّ زَيْدًا</span>, both meaning the same [i. e. <i>I saw
'Amr: then Zeyd</i>]: (TA:) and in like manner
one says <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُمَّتَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">فُمَّتْ</span>, meaning <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُمَّتَ</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تُمَّتْ</span>.
(M and TA voce <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُمَّ</span>.)

